From: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Date: Sat, 9 May 2026 21:09:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: Add RSS support

Add support for Receive Side Scaling.

We can adjust SMP affinity with the following command:
echo [CPU bitmap num] > /proc/irq/[virtual IRQ ID]/smp_affinity,
with interrupts evenly assigned to 4 CPUs, we were able to measure
an RX throughput of 7.3Gbps using iperf3 on the MT7988. Further
optimizations will be carried out in the future.

The experimental command is as follows:
PC: iperf3 -c [IP] -P 10
DUT: iperf3 -s

The entire indirection table can be imagined as 128 buckets, we
can use the ethtool command to mark which RX ring we want to send
the packets in these buckets to.

Show RSS RX ring parameters in indirection table and RSS hash key:
ethtool -x [interface]
Change RSS RX rings weight under uniform distribution:
ethtool --set-rxfh-indir [interface] equal [ring num]
Change RSS RX rings weight under non-uniform distribution:
ethtool --set-rxfh-indir [interface] weight [ring0 weight]
[ring1 weight] [ring2 weight] [ring3 weight]

Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/netdevbpf/patch/20260509190938.169290-3-linux@fw-web.de/
Signed-off-by: Mason Chang <mason-cw.chang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Frank Wunderlich <frank-w@public-files.de>
[plcharriere: port to Linux 6.18 with OpenWrt's patches and address the
review of v8: use RSS only when the SoC sets rss_num and the device tree
provides the pdma0 to pdma3 interrupts, instead of new capability bits,
so other SoCs and older device trees keep one RX ring; use BIT(24 + ring)
as RX done only with RSS, as MediaTek's SDK does, and keep the existing
RX done bits otherwise; give each ring its own Net DIM counters and let
one ring at a time sample them; handle MTK_INT_STATUS2 from ring 0 only;
program the RX delay interrupt of RSS rings 0 and 1 in addition to the
existing delay registers; keep the HW LRO ring polling; fill the hash key
with netdev_rss_key_fill() and keep the key and indirection table across
restarts; reject indirection entries beyond the last ring and pause RSS
while ethtool changes them; report the ring count through get_rxnfc; name
the ring interrupts and spread them over the CPUs; leave MT7988 without
RSS; drop the unused rxd7 read and the LRO register macro changes]
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Co-developed-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
